    "question": {
      ":question/id": "4ab6255a-2668-509c-9456-b75fdf8371c2",
      ":question/problem": "Given that $F(x,y,z)=7{z}^{2}\\,i+2y\\,j+k,$ what is $\\text{curl}\\,F?$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "If $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j+R\\,k$ is a vector field on ${R}^{3}$ and the partial derivatives of the components of $F$ all exist, then the curl of $F$ is the vector field given by\n\n$$\ncurl\\,F=\u2207\\times F=|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\frac{\u2202}{\u2202x} & \\frac{\u2202}{\u2202y} & \\frac{\u2202}{\u2202z} \\\\ P & Q & R\\end{aligned}|.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{curl}\\,F & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\frac{\u2202}{\u2202x} & \\frac{\u2202}{\u2202y} & \\frac{\u2202}{\u2202z} \\\\ 7{z}^{2} & 2y & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =[\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202y}(1)-\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202z}(2y)]i-[\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202x}(1)-\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202z}(7{z}^{2})]j+[\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202x}(2y)-\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202y}(7{z}^{2})]k \\\\  & =(0-0)i-(0-14z)j+(0-0)k \\\\  & =14z\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
